      "text": "Yes, and they really help. Start with simple ones, like standing on one foot while holding a sturdy chair."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.8,
      "end": 24.63,
      "text": "Safety first, especially after a fall. As he gets steadier, he can hold on with just one finger."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 27.43,
      "end": 34.56,
      "text": "Heel to toe walking along a hallway, and sit to stand from a chair without using his hands. Both build strength and balance."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.13,
      "end": 49.83,
      "text": "Maybe frame it as staying independent rather than exercising. A tai chi class for seniors is also excellent for balance."
    },
    {
